WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:04.020
<i>Led by a strange old man named Myr,</i>

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.150
<i>Seth met Ocoho,
 a Knight-sorcerer applicant.</i>

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.900
<i>But as they were battling 
a Spectral Nemesis,</i>

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.990
<i>Seth fell off their dragon's back
 while protecting Ocoho.</i>

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.120
Seth?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.870
Seth!

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.980
Contact has been severed!

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.370
Hand off to the nearest dragon
 standing by!

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.320
Out of the way, Ocoho!

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.330
U-Um, my pilot fell off.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.260
You broke out of the Gysoni spell!
 You're in the way!

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.010
Seth...

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:14.980
<b>The Bringer of Calamity 
-Dullahan-</b>

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:13.850
<i>"The Bringer of Calamity."</i>

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.110
It's terrifying.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.420
Come on. We have to get farther away.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.930
But we can't just leave 
the field like that.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.410
Dad, look!

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.270
Th-That was scary.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:46.350
I still can't gather Fantasia 
with my left hand.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.000
Is it because Torque's blade struck it?

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.980
My right hand... seems to work fine.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.610
Wow! A Knight-sorcerer with horns!

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.090
There can't be a knight with horns.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.170
Hey! What are you guys doing?

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.010
There's a Nemesis over there!

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.620
We know!

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.870
We saw it appear out of nowhere!

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.430
Out of nowhere?

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:15.380
Didn't an egg fall out of the sky first?

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.850
No way, no how.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:22.640
We were plowing the field 
when suddenly, there it was!

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.730
What on earth...

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.330
Anyway, it's dangerous here!

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.870
Seth!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.020
Ocoho!

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.770
I'm so glad you're okay!

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:37.780
Well, sure—

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.030
Ocoho! I give! I give! I give!

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:46.530
Why did you try to take 
that attack bare-handed?!

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.230
Well...
 I couldn't get my magic to work right.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.820
You should've dodged it, then!

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.870
That's why I gave you the reins!

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.090
Ow, ow, ow!

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:02.280
What was that?
 An attack from the Nemesis?

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.350
No. Look up.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.290
Their magic's going right through it!

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:18.060
They're weakening it,
 before launching the final attack.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.760
Oh, no...
 And it was ready to harvest, too...

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.880
It was ready...

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.340
We're being punished because you decided
 to bargain with that foreigner!

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.370
Wh-What?!

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.690
It's not punishment.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.790
Dad, you saw the Dullahan, right?

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.290
It's the curse.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.590
The curse!

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:41.300
The "Dullahan"?

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.750
Seth, we have to get away from here.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.390
The next attack is coming.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.810
Seth?!

00:04:58.450 --> 00:04:59.840
It's hard to move in this!

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.070
Repulse!

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.330
That's so cool!
 What the heck is that shield?!

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.220
What are you doing?

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.850
Can't you even use a Dome of Protection?

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.420
But as long as you have that,

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.590
attacks from the sky can't hit us!

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.720
I never received any such order.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.180
Order? What order?

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.750
Did you get an order
 to attack and destroy this farm?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.540
Of course not!

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.730
Our mission is to defeat the Nemesis!

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.840
So you don't care what you
 have to do to accomplish that?

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.240
Even if you destroy farms 
people need to survive?

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.290
That makes you no better 
than the Nemesis!

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.730
It's more than just saving people's lives.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.580
Without this farm, people will starve.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.880
I'm going to fight.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.010
What about you?

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.300
All right.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.460
I'm going to use Cromen. Help me.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.580
"Cromen"?

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.290
It's a spell to protect a large area.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:28.200
But the more sorcerers there are to cast it, 
even just one, the more effective it is.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.530
Okay.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.270
Here goes.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.450
Cromen!

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.580
What just happened?!

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.550
Our power is being sucked away.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:52.050
<i>What is this?
 It's as if I'm in a sea of Fantasia.</i>

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:55.560
<i>He can gather Fantasia 
in such immense amounts?</i>

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.650
<i>Just who is he?!</i>

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:02.100
<i>Lord Brangoire,
 the Gysoni spell is about to be broken!</i>

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.590
It seems that dome
 is swallowing all the Fantasia.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:12.490
Mordred!
 The Nemesis is starting to disappear!

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.070
Let's attack it quickly.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:15.580
Right.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:32.340
I guess it worked.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.600
But that was one strange Nemesis.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.620
What a mess...

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:48.680
And it was almost ready to harvest, too.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.610
We can't sell any of this.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.430
Thanks to all of your efforts,

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:01.910
we have successfully defeated
 the Spectral Nemesis.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.100
Well done!

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:09.170
You are certain to become
 fine Knights-sorcerers.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.670
However...

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.300
The only ones who will be truly great

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:17.930
are Mordred and Sagramore here.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:21.020
The rest of you are useless scum!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.670
Why did you break formation 
and cease attacking?!

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.940
You think you can become
 Knights-sorcerers that way?!

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:31.070
W-With all due respect, 
Lord Brangoire...

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:36.030
We didn't have enough Fantasia at that time.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.410
What?!

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:41.930
I think it was because of the magic
 Ocoho used on the ground.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:43.660
I agree!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:45.280
You bastard!

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.420
You used magic on the ground?!

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:50.270
Why would you do such a thing 
without my permission?!

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:51.990
Answer me, Ocoho!

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.690
Um... I'm Ocoho.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:55.550
Huh?!

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.120
Damn you!

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.250
How many times must I say it?!

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.310
You people are nothing on your own!

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:08.980
Your individual thoughts
 and abilities are useless in battle!

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:09.730
But—

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.320
No excuses!

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:15.500
Did you just want
 to be in the spotlight?

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:19.700
If that's the case, then be a minstrel 
or an acrobat instead of a knight!

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:23.330
And go join the clowns over 
at Artemis or something!

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.650
Have you forgotten
 the great Merlin's teachings?!

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:30.000
What's important is not the individual,
 but harmonious teamwork!

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.590
That means Gysoni!

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:35.470
I see you haven't changed, Brangoire.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.340
That voice...

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.410
Y-Your Highness!

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:47.980
<b>[Gysoni] 
A magic that synchronizes your senses with others.
 Harmonizing allows you to demonstrate
 power exceeding your individual abilities.</b>

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:56.350
Her Highness Queen Boudica has arrived!

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.310
Knights! Bow to your queen!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.870
What's this?

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:07.750
Why are you kneeling with only one knee?

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:11.100
Oh! F-Forgive me, Your Highness!

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:14.880
She's huge! Is that a curse, too?

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:20.060
Your Highness, I did not expect you 
to appear in a place like this!

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:22.090
I beg your forgiveness!

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:23.760
Quite all right.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.630
I'm only paying a little visit.

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:29.610
But why are you in such a position?

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:30.650
Your Highness?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:34.650
You'll be able to see up my skirt.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.150
P-Please forgive me!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.660
I wanted to see the Spectral Nemesis.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:47.200
It has caused my people to suffer,
 has it not?

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.160
Yes!

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:51.940
My people's suffering is my own.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:56.420
What a dreadful thing
 I have put you through.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:11:00.100
Y-You are too kind, Your Highness.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:02.680
I thank you for your concern.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:06.080
It's true that our fields were damaged,

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.060
but thanks to the knights,
 they weren't completely destroyed.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.290
I'm so glad to hear that.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:15.500
But your head should be just a bit lower.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:23.320
Y-Your Highness... We are frightened.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.330
Hey! How dare you directly address the queen?!

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.050
I will hear his plea.

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:29.290
Your Highness?!

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:32.340
Brangoire, your head.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:37.210
My people's pain is my own.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:41.460
What has frightened all of you so?

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:44.900
Well... When night falls,

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.490
the Dullahan always shows up!

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:48.870
The "Dullahan"?

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.850
It's a terrifying spirit
 that carries its head in its arms.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:56.210
It started showing up in this area

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:58.920
around the same time
 the Spectral Nemesis did.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:00.260
Oh, dear...

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:05.070
Is there anything else
 you know about the Dullahan?

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:10.330
Well, it's been called the Bringer of Calamity.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.500
"Calamity," you say?

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:15.850
Your Highness...

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:19.410
First the Spectrals,
 and now the Dullahan...

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:23.590
Why must we endure such misfortune?

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.650
My people, listen well.

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:36.290
Through the efforts
 of my late husband, Prasutag,

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:40.570
the many years of war that had 
plagued this land came to an end.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:44.900
We had finally attained peace, 
fleeting though it was.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:51.580
However, regrettably, something has brought 
war to this land once again.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:54.330
The Spectral Nemesis and the Dullahan...

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:59.590
I do not yet know
 what these things mean for us.

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:04.620
However, I must listen to all beings
 of this world.

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:09.600
I'm sure the spirit of the great Merlin
 must be trembling right now.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.530
And why is that?

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:16.810
This is something
 that each of you must ask yourselves.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:21.730
Are we worthy
 to follow in the great Merlin's footsteps?

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:24.940
Do we understand the things he said?

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:30.990
Can we protect the land of 
Cyfandir as he did?

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.910
No, not just the land.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:38.250
We must protect all of the lives within it.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:41.900
Ocoho.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.660
As Brangoire said,

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:50.150
what you did
 could have caused a grave situation.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:55.890
However, your actions were befitting 
of the great Merlin's will.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.270
Your Highness...

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:01.930
This land that you so bravely protected

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:04.420
should now be entrusted 
to these farmers.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:09.340
I'm certain this land
 will one day be fruitful again.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.010
Would you agree?

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:13.410
Yes! Most definitely!

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:19.540
Now, I must return
 to my official duties.

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:23.180
Brangoire, forgive my intrusion.

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:28.300
You and your soldiers all fought splendidly.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.320
Thank you, Your Highness!

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:33.090
Brangoire...

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:37.370
You mustn't lift your face yet.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:39.840
Oh! I didn't mean to!

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.980
Please forgive me!

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:45.620
Be well, everyone.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:49.630
I pray the great Merlin's protection
 will be with you.

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:53.580
Her Highness the Queen is now departing!

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:02.040
The queen always looks so beautiful!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:03.380
She smells so nice.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.180
I wish she'd pat my head, too.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:07.380
I'll never wash my face again.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:10.670
H-Hey! Stop staring at the queen!

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.770
We're going back to the castle!

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:14.470
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:17.100
We're finally going back.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:18.630
Seth!

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:21.220
Hey, did you see that? 
Were you watching?!

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:25.620
The queen knew my name!

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:28.860
I-I know! I know! Put me down!

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:33.550
Oh, gosh!
 I bet I just earned some points!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.340
Lord Brangoire was pretty mad, though.

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:39.570
But he's always like that!

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:41.780
I mean, the queen praised me!

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:44.130
Now I'm sure to be ordained!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.560
Draccoon!

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:48.110
We'll celebrate with 
a double serving of fruit today!

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:51.620
No, make it triple!

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:54.510
He has a weird call.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:56.280
Well, ready to head back?

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:59.290
There are lots of things 
I want to ask you,

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.270
but first, let's celebrate!

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:02.390
Sure...

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:05.660
Seth?

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:09.400
Uh, I just remembered
 there's something I need to do!

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.270
Sorry. Go on without me.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.420
Really?

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:14.110
See you later, then.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:15.530
S-Sure!

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:26.540
Hey, Grimm, what the heck
 are you doing there?

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.670
Ah, so you knew it was Grimm?

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:33.010
Uh, it would've been pretty hard not to.

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:39.080
What's not weird about a guy covered 
in bandages standing around like this?

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:40.990
You are curious about Grimm?

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:42.190
Well, sorta.

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:45.770
It'd definitely be handy
 if I could erase my presence like you.

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:49.600
Grimm impersonates a scarecrow in fields,

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:51.890
becomes a ghost in graveyards,

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:55.780
and takes the guise of a sick, 
exhausted traveler on roadsides.

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:59.280
From your perspective,
 perhaps it does seem strange.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.540
Yeah.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:05.540
People are unaware of things
 that fall outside their own interests.

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:09.050
Even if they see them with their own eyes,

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:11.410
they forget the things
 that have no value to them.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:14.050
Much like Grimm right now.

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:19.070
This is something Grimm can achieve
 by maintaining a distance from the world.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:23.310
Is that what you wish you could have?

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:28.920
Besides, you do not need
 to be like Grimm.

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.070
You succeeded in sneaking 
into the castle,

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:33.350
putting yourself
 in an advantageous position.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:36.580
That castle is not an easy place
 to get into.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.980
Yeah, but it's what comes after that.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:42.570
There might be information 
on Radiant in the library,

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:45.490
but I can't get inside
 unless I join those knights.

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:48.710
Hm... The library, you say?

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.100
What about it?

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:53.080
Grimm has a favor to ask of you.

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:54.610
What is it?

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:56.590
You've helped me lots of times.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.050
If there's anything I can do for you,
 just ask.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:03.430
There is something 
 Grimm wants in that castle.

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:06.180
You want me to steal it?!

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:08.650
I can't do that!

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.820
No. Only to borrow it for a bit.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.650
Look at this.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.440
What is it?

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:19.090
This is a memory stone.

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:23.550
Certain sorcerers wear stones 
like this one at all times.

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:28.900
It has the unique ability
 to record its owner's experiences.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:31.460
Huh... It's pretty.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:36.080
There is something in the castle library
 called the Anmatheque.

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.760
"A-Anuma"...?

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:42.770
It is a collection of memory stones 
used by great sorcerers of the past.

00:18:42.770 --> 00:18:46.930
Among them is a stone
 used by a female sorcerer named Magosia.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.270
Do you think you can find it
 and sneak it out?

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.740
I'm not sure about that.

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:55.570
Can't you go in
 and get it yourself, Grimm?

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.940
Grimm cannot enter the castle walls.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:01.150
Huh? Why not?

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:03.970
Because Grimm is Grimm.

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:06.080
I don't get it.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:09.390
What are you gonna use that stone for, anyway?

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:10.620
For something.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.950
What "something"?

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.250
Something means something.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.850
Okay, fine! I get it!

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:20.240
I owe you, after all.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:23.970
I have no idea how I'm gonna sneak
 into the library, though.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.010
Hm, that is true.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.060
Hey!

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:30.430
Perhaps you are not suited for espionage.

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:33.720
That girl who always traveled with you

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:38.320
or the boy with the man's soul 
might be better for the job.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:41.320
Melie and Doc...

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:46.230
Incidentally, why are you not traveling
 with them now?

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:51.330
They have already arrived
 in Caislean Merlin, have they not?

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:54.060
You know everything, huh?

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:58.810
I did see them,
 but they were acting strange.

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:03.180
Personally, Grimm thinks all of it
 is strange, including you.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:05.390
I don't mean that kind of strange!

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:07.870
It was just... I mean...

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:10.420
Like there was this weird distance
 between us.

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:16.980
Maybe they're angry because 
I left Artemis without telling them.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:21.360
Seth, you left without
 telling the two of them?

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:25.070
Yeah...
 I did leave a note for them, though.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:30.910
Such an act is bound to cause unwanted 
misunderstandings and disagreements.

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:33.630
What do you think I should do?

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:36.460
Unfortunately, Grimm has no idea.

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:38.800
For some reason,

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:42.120
Grimm seems to be a master
 at causing unwanted misunderstandings.

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.550
I think I can guess why.

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:50.010
Besides, is this really a question 
that an outsider should answer?

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:55.220
No... I need to solve this one
 on my own, huh?

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:59.290
In that case, if the cheap inn
 called the Luchorpan has vacancies,

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:00.610
you should stay there.

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:03.320
All other places are too expensive.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:06.090
Okay. Thanks.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:07.550
I'll check it out later.

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:10.230
You know, Grimm...

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:14.690
You really seem to know a lot
 about Caislean Merlin.

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:18.080
You knew about the castle library,
 and that inn.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:19.930
Is that so?

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:23.090
Were you once a Knight-sorcerer
 or something?

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:24.630
No.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:26.620
That's all you have to say?

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:29.100
You're always so mysterious.

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:31.600
Grimm is Grimm.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:36.030
I'm pretty curious about
 what's under those bandages, though.

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:38.600
Hey, Grimm...

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.070
Not again!

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:47.020
Jeez...
 He never tells me anything about himself.

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:52.870
The Luchorpan, huh?

00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:56.100
Guess I'll check it out.

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:08.630
Man, I'm drunk as a skunk.

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:11.710
What's wrong?

00:22:13.110 --> 00:22:13.940
Look...

00:22:19.490 --> 00:22:22.830
Th-The Dullahan!

00:22:25.630 --> 00:22:29.990
To Be Continued

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:20.740
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:00.590 --> 00:24:02.330
<i>After getting Grimm's advice,</i>

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:06.610
<i>Seth makes up his mind
 to talk to Melie and Doc again.</i>

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:10.010
<i>But when he visits the inn,</i>

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:12.910
<i>for some reason,
 Melie treats him coldly.</i>

00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:16.950
<i>Melie feels hurt by Seth,
 who doesn't understand what's going on,</i>

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:18.930
<i>and she says goodbye to him.</i>

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:24.170
<i>Next time on <i>Radiant</i>,
"Silent Rain, Distant Hearts."</i>

00:24:20.740 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>Silent Rain, Distant Hearts 
-Rain-</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>Draccoon?!</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>Seems to like Seth.</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>End</b>
